---
title: Proposition 31
---
order: 31
---
short_label: IX.31
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If an odd number is relatively prime to any number, then it is also relatively prime to double it.
----
proof:

Let the odd number *A* be relatively prime to any number *B,* and let *C* be double of *B.*

I say that *A* is relatively prime to *C.*

